                <pb facs="0105" n="73" xml:id="pg73"/>

                <head>44. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On March 28, <hi rendition="#italic">The New York Times</hi> published a story on
                    Cuba which, among other things, noted that the U.S. Government had recently
                    embargoed a shipment of rifles to the Cuban Government. (March 28, 1958, <ref
                        target="#pg9">page 9</ref>) For Wieland’s recollection of how <hi rendition="#italic">The New
                        York Times</hi> obtained the information, see his testimony of February 2,
                    1962, before a Senate subcommittee. (<hi rendition="#italic">State Department
                        Security: Testimony of William
                            Wieland</hi>, Hearings Before the Subcommittee to Investigate
                    the Administration of the Internal Security Act and Other Internal Security Laws
                    of the Committee on the Judiciary, United States Senate, 87th Congress
                    (Washington: U.S. Government Printing Office, 1962), page 659)</p>
            </div>
